    description: "Andy Weir's Project Hail Mary opens on Ryland Grace waking in a spacecraft with no memory of how he got there, two dead crewmates, and equipment that tells him he is not in the solar system where he started. The novel is structured around Grace's memories returning as he works the problem of his mission — and around what happens when he discovers he is not alone in this system. The science is as accurate as Weir can make it; the humor is consistent; and the central relationship of the novel — between Grace and a being from another star system — is one of the most unusual partnerships in recent fiction. If the problem-solving, the optimism about what intelligence can accomplish when it cooperates, and the relationship at the novel's center gripped you, these eight picks go to the same place.",
