    description: "Leo Tolstoy's The Death of Ivan Ilyich (1886) is the most concentrated literary examination of a life wrongly lived — Ivan Ilyich's dying recognition that he has spent his life doing what was expected of him rather than what was true. At 80 pages, the most efficient moral work in Tolstoy's output. These novels will find you in the same territory.",
    keywords: ['books like The Death of Ivan Ilyich Leo Tolstoy', 'books like Death of Ivan Ilyich', 'tolstoy similar books', 'existential fiction similar books', 'what to read after Death of Ivan Ilyich', 'leo tolstoy recommendations'],
